  "body": "I want to use CamCraft for simultaneous 5-axis machining on my self-built XYZAC milling machine.\n\nThe machine has an AC rotary table and is controlled by Mach4 with a PoKeys CNC controller. My intended application is finishing the internal freeform chamber of saxophone mouthpieces, including undercuts, with ball-nose and lollipop cutters.\n\nCamCraft already generates simultaneous 5-axis tool-tip paths, and the post collection contains Mach4 and MachMotion posts. However, these posts currently enable `G43.4` and expect the controller to perform RTCP/pivot compensation.\n\nStandard Mach4 does not provide this RTCP workflow. For true simultaneous 5-axis machining, my machine needs final, already-compensated `X Y Z A C` coordinates and `G93` inverse-time feed generated by the CAM/postprocessor.",
